<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunker final report and prices -April 10.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunker final report and prices -April 10.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DELIVERED U.S.$/TONNE)  380 CST   180 CST     MDO     GAS OIL</p>
<p> SINGAPORE CARGO	    93/94     98/99	UNQ     199/202</p>
<p> SINGAPORE BUNKER	   98/99    105/106   198/200   212/215</p>
<p>--------</p>
<p>COMMENTS - The spread between Singapore 180-cst/380-cst bunker fuel oil widened by $1/$2 per tonne on Thursday due to tight supplies of the 180-cst grade, traders said. &quot;It's very expensive to blend the 380-cst grade into the 180-cst grade,&quot; said one trader. &quot;Some suppliers simply don't offer the 180-cst grade.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3571)</p>
